[
  {
    "sha": "51c85c2e512f6124f6fe0abeb2702a8e113a452f",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVoU8JdoAKDUxYzg1YzJlNTEyZjYxMjRmNmZlMGFiZWIyNzAyYThlMTEzYTQ1MmY",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-19T02:34:24Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-19T02:34:24Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(deburr): picked and excluded edges, minimum edge angle, hole filter\n\nA 3D Deburr now breaks only the picked edge chains when its source is a\nselection, leaves out the chains in `exclude_edges`, skips a convex\ncrease that bends less than `min_edge_angle_deg`, and skips the rims of\nrecognized round holes inside a diameter range.\n\n- motion: `finishing3d::deburr_edges` and the `deburr_filter` module.\n  `deburr` keeps its behaviour with the filters at rest.\n- app: the new `OpParams::Deburr` fields with their sanity door, seed,\n  stamp digest and project-file keys (absent at rest, so an old file\n  reads and saves unchanged). `operation/deburr_picks.rs` resolves the\n  picked and the excluded chains. The MCP pick door takes edge chains\n  only for a Deburr.\n- ui: the Deburr Geometry tab has the minimum edge angle, the hole\n  filter and the excluded-edge list.\n\nA pick that names no rim or convex crease is refused by name. A pick\nthat is not an edge chain is refused by name.\n\nFixes #1888\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
