      "message": "fix(deburr): read a directed hole's wall span by its travel sign\n\nAfter the merge of main (#2601), a `CrossHole` wall point at travel `d`\nstands at `origin - dir * d`. The hole filter read the span with the\nother sign and matched only the mouth ring. The far rim of a cross hole\nstayed in the ride. The span now uses the negated travel scalars, and a\ncross-hole test pins the two rims.\n\nRefs #1888\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
